invariant: INV-39
file: srv_tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-nonblocking server answers a ClientHello that has bytes
  after it in its record with a ServerHello, and reads those bytes under
  the client's handshake key afterwards. RFC 9846 section 5.1 makes that
  unexpected_message. test/tcp_nonblocking_record_end_tests.h adds one byte
  to the ClientHello's record and requires that alert and no ServerHello.

--- old
    int rc = hsr_check_record_end(h);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
    rc = srv_send_server_hello(h, ch, sel);
--- new
    int rc = srv_send_server_hello(h, ch, sel);
